  "term": "dimethyltryptamine",
  "definition": "Dimethyltryptamine is a naturally occurring indoleamine found in several plant species and in very small amounts in mammalian brain, blood, and urine. It is a serotonergic hallucinogen that can act on certain serotonin receptors as either an agonist or an antagonist.",
